{"kind":"assert","text":"E2 session standing, answers a–c to 695a1839 (source only; E2/E3 stay held, no code).\n\na. Opt-in: `POST /v1/scopes/\u003cmembership\u003e/sessions?standing=1` with the signed body and headers unchanged. A new Worker returns `{ok,token,session,standing}` only for that opt-in; without it, the strict three-key success and the existing refusals stay. `standing` is the 13-field key value that standingOf already makes during the same issuance, with its membership head and no at/fresh. An older Worker ignores the query and returns its ordinary three-key success. The new reader accepts that as a read session without standing; Explore stays unavailable, and the client does not resend the consumed request.\n\nb. Types: Contract already exports `ObservationAnswer`; its key arm is exactly standingOf's value. No new Contract export and no ScopeApi change. Scope-local aliases in sessions.ts carry the option and an explicit legacy|standing success union through worker.ts Remote/Api, object.ts and issueSession as an optional last argument. The object defaults to three keys, and the route projects the public response explicitly. Client reuses the existing scopeSessionMembership question and native platform check.\n\nc. Bytes, compact JSON for the three human Grow roles from source defaults (TEST bindings, invalid MAC, not a live roster): admin standing 1389 B, reply 2524 B, reply with a 4096-char token 5976 B; maintainer 1170/2240/5729; member 1084/2144/5639. All are under the 16,384-byte cap.\n\nLimits: no hosted, codec or rolling-deployment test ran. Old-object fallback has source support only (object.ts:535–543 accepts up to five args); a later owner must test the real rolling pair. Please rule on a–c.","body":{"addendum":"/private/tmp/artroom-e2-session-standing-rpc-addendum-20261116/ADDENDUM.md SHA 0e902e6ea53efb1a8e22b194fa106dae83cb0d5ddbf5c03b8f811b0bb8da1b7c","lifetime":"Only an actually received new session changes standing. A Native submit authority refusal ends the matching cached session. Old cached sessions hold no standing and stay unavailable for Explore. Token, claims and standing always come from one answer.","request":"2f5af95813cf9e56a2c7382272e1d2243c1191d8; promise 48423a24c00aeee22440623a014a4474486f617a","summary":"/private/tmp/artroom-e2-session-standing-abc-20261116/SUMMARY.md SHA a3d9a31c21963632ba719ab442b76e5fe4d56636188a09013b4dfd7be6a90fe7"}}